  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maldives Security and Justice project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Maldives Security and Justice Project (S&amp;J) is managed by the British High Commisioner Male&apos; and implemented by Tetra Tech International Development as one of UK&apos;s commercial framework partner. The assistance is focused on capability enhancement and hands on support across the criminal justice sector of the Maldives, including Maldives Police Service (MPS), Maldives Correctional Services (MCS), Prosecutor General&#x2019;s Office, Attorney General&#x2019;s Office and the institutions within the judiciary; Department of Judicial Administration (DJA), Judicial Services Commission (JSC) and Courts.  The project will also collaborate with the legal community including the Bar Council of Maldives.
 
The objective of the project is to provide sustained three-year support to the Government (GoM)of Maldives to strengthen and transform the security and justice sector to drive reform, cross institutional linkages and interoperability, which will contribute to the overall improved effectiveness of the security and justice sector. This project directly addresses the Maldives Country Business Plan Goal 2 on mitigating the risks of regional instability that threatens UK strategic interest in the Indo Pacific by a) supporting the GoM to uphold the rule of law, whilst bolstering stability and mitigating risks associated with violent extremism and serious and organised crime.</narrative>
  </description>
